.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH tensor-wasm-run 1  "tensor-wasm-run " 
.SH NAME
tensor\-wasm\-run \- Run a Wasm module locally against the in\-process TensorWasm engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtensor\-wasm\-run\fR [\fB\-\-export\fR] [\fB\-\-args\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIFILE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run a Wasm module locally against the in\-process TensorWasm engine
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-export\fR \fI<EXPORT>\fR [default: main]
Name of the exported function to call. Defaults to `main`
.TP
\fB\-\-args\fR \fI<ARGS>\fR
Arguments to pass to the export, encoded as a JSON array.

Example: `\-\-args \*(Aq[1.0, 2.0]\*(Aq`. The current executor only invokes `() \-> ()` exports, so the array is parsed and validated but the values are not yet wired into the call site.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIFILE\fR>
Path to the `.wasm` file to execute
